curl has closed down it's bug bounty program because of the wave of AI slop PRs. They are following a trend of open source projects that have pulled back from easy contribution. The programming language Zig had already moved off of github. Tldraw closed all PRs that are not requested by maintainers or from a trusted contributor. Drupal used to have a verified status that was required to create a new module. It was a beast of a procrocess. It was full of insider baseball type of wheeling and dealing as much as it was a technical review. I went through this process and my feedback to them, at the time, was "if I had to do this before having invested years into Drupal I would not be using Drupal today."
The issue facing the Drupal project then was cost of infrastructure was so high that they couldn't afford to just let anyone flood their servers with garbage. There needed to be a gatekeeper. The open contribution model was one that worked when the work itself is a gateway. This isn't much more of the case. But the real issue for these Open Source projects is that the contributions are not good enough to justify the volume. They aren't good enough because the people that are pushing these contributions do not know that they do not know how to program.
